<title>BELGIUM: Belgian industrial output down 0.1% yr/yr in Nov.</title>
<headline>Belgian industrial output down 0.1% yr/yr in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Statistics Office released the following indices for production in industry excluding the construction sector -</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	    Nov 96     Oct 96	   Nov 95</p>
<p> work day index (1990=100) (*)   108.6     100.7	    108.6</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) index per working day, adjusted for length and composition of the months</p>
<p> SEASONALLY ADJUSTED INDICES(*) Nov 96     Oct 96	   Nov 95</p>
<p> industry as a whole		 94.5	 94.6	     94.4</p>
<p> construction industry	     76.2	 76.7	     81.0</p>
<p> investment goods		   100.1	100.5	     98.8</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) seasonally adjusted based on averages of the last 12 months.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
